course: dictionary
lesson: 14184
title: One colour, many shades
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts that give you clues. Monochrome is built from «mono», which means one, and «chrome», which means colour. So monochrome means one colour, or shades of one colour. «The artist painted the harbour in monochrome, using only shades of grey.» The clue is «only shades of grey», so monochrome means using just one colour family.
explain: Monochrome can also be a noun, meaning a picture, photo or screen in black and white or one colour. «Grandma's first television was a monochrome, so everything looked black, white and grey.» Here the word names the screen itself.
explain: Monochrome can also mean dull and without variety. «The rainy town felt monochrome, all grey buildings and grey skies.» The author is not talking only about colour here. The grey makes the place feel boring and flat. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking, does it still make sense?
fact: Monochrome means using only one colour or shades of one colour, especially black, white and grey.
fact: «Mono» means one, and «chrome» means colour, so the word is built from two parts you can look for.
fact: As a noun, a monochrome is a picture, photo or screen in black and white or one colour.
fact: Old televisions were monochrome, which means they showed pictures in black, white and grey.
fact: «Monochrome» can also describe something dull and without variety, such as «a monochrome town».
exercise: «The artist painted the harbour in monochrome, using only shades of grey.» What does monochrome mean here? | *Using only one colour or shades of one colour | Painted in a hurry | Full of bright rainbow colours | Very large and very old
exercise: «Grandma's first television was monochrome, so everything looked black, white and grey.» Find and copy the words that name the colours. | *black, white and grey | everything looked | television | Grandma's first
exercise: Which of these could be called a monochrome picture? | *An old photo in black, white and grey | A map with red, green and blue countries | A bright poster of a jungle full of parrots | A rainbow painted over the hills
test:
«Her outfit was monochrome: a black top, a grey skirt and white shoes.» What does monochrome mean in this sentence? | Covered in spots | *All one colour, or shades of one colour | Very expensive and shiny | Bright and colourful
«The rainy town felt monochrome, all grey buildings and grey skies.» What does monochrome suggest about the town? | Loud, busy and full of music | Warm and sunny | *Dull and without variety | Full of bright flowers
exam: «The dull, monochrome town made Maya long for some colour.» What does monochrome suggest about the town? | *Dull and without variety | Warm and sunny | Happy and full of colour | Loud and noisy
